        <item>
            <title>0.15.32</title>
            <pubDate>Tue, 07 Jul 2026 12:10:42 +0100</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>193</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.15.32</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.2</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<ul>
<li>Recording your voice through headphones/AirPods after switching to them mid-call no longer plays back sped-up. 0.15.28 fixed one cause but missed the audio resampler, which was being finalised after the first buffer — so all the headphone audio after that collapsed. Verified the resampler now keeps the right length across the whole stream.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
